    <briefdescription>
<para>Provides a cast trait that uses a defined pointer to pointer cast as a base for reference-to-reference casts. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Note that it does not provide castFailed and doCastIfPossible because a pointer-to-pointer cast would likely just return <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> which could cause nullptr dereference. You can use it like this:</para>
<para>template &lt;&gt; struct <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_info" kindref="compound">CastInfo&lt;foo, bar *&gt;</ref> { ... verbose implementation... };</para>
<para>template &lt;&gt; struct <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_cast_info" kindref="compound">CastInfo&lt;foo, bar&gt;</ref> : public <ref refid="structllvm_1_1_forward_to_pointer_cast" kindref="compound">ForwardToPointerCast&lt;foo, bar, CastInfo&lt;foo, bar *&gt;&gt;</ref> {}; </para>
    </detaileddescription>
